ry has 233 thousand cases of Kovan  19 the fourth highest number of cases in  the world other Latin American countries  that are locked down are also struggling  Peru took action early shutting down  borders in March and even limiting which  days people could leave their homes it  now has more than 80,000 kovin 19 cases  and there's particular concern about the  spread of the corona virus in markets at  one produce market in the capital 79% of  vendors have tested positive for the  illness and then there's El Salvador it  enacted some of the toughest Kovan 19  restrictions even before it had a single  case it now has about 1300 human rights  groups have accused the president of  abusing power amid the pandemic more  than 7,000 people have been detained in  cramped containment centers after  returning to the country or for  violating quarantine measures it's fear  the virus is spreading among the  detainees but the government isn't  revealing how many of them have tested  positive or how many have died coming up  between an activist and a former  president their messages to the class of  2020  normally this time of year is filled  with graduation events instead the class  of 2020 is taking part in a virtual  graduation tonight we honor 12 years of  your hard work  this special called graduate together  America honors the high school class of  2020 was hosted by NBA star LeBron James  a number of musicians actors and  activists came together last night to  celebrate grads including Malala  yousufzai the class of 2020 won't be  defined by what we lost to his finest  but by how we responded to it the world  is yours now  former US President Barack Obama had the  final remarks of the night in his speech  he called on graduates to shape the  future he also took a dig at his  successor you know all those adults they  used to think or in charge and knew what  they were doing turns out they don't  have all the answers do what you think  is right doing what feels good what's 